.TH ORYN 1 "October 2026" "oryn 0.1.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oryn \- terminal hardware monitor with every temperature sensor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oryn
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oryn
shows every temperature sensor in the machine (CPU, GPU with hotspot and
VRAM chips, RAM, NVMe, SATA and USB drives, chipset, network cards) in one
table, with btop-style panels for CPU, GPU, memory, disks, network,
processes and system specs.
.PP
A few readings need root: SMART drive temperatures, RAM part numbers, CPU
power draw and the hotspot of NVIDIA RTX 50 cards. Run \fBsudo oryn\fR for those; your own
user's settings are used either way.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Use simulated sensors (virtual machines, containers, trying the interface).
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print every detected sensor once and exit.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " \fIms\fR"
Refresh interval in milliseconds, 100 to 10000 (default 1000).
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Color scheme, e.g. \fBdracula\fR, \fBnord\fR, \fBtokyo-night\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-themes
List the 100 available color schemes.
.TP
.BI \-\-panels " list"
Panels to show: a comma list of \fBsensors\fR, \fBhistory\fR, \fBcpu\fR,
\fBmem\fR, \fBdisks\fR, \fBnet\fR, \fBproc\fR, \fBgpu\fR, \fBspecs\fR, or
\fBall\fR; a leading \fB\-\fR hides one (\fBall,\-proc\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Start in compact mode: temperatures only, no graphs or bars.
.TP
.B \-\-gpu\-info
Explain which NVIDIA hotspot and VRAM temperatures can be read, and why not.
.TP
.B \-\-ram\-info
Explain what was read for RAM names, speed and timings, and where it stopped (FreeBSD).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-nvapi
Don't load NVIDIA's NvAPI library.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q, Esc
Quit.
.TP
.B \(ua \(da, k j
Select a sensor (its history is graphed).
.TP
.B Tab
Move the keys between the sensor table and the process list.
.TP
.B PgUp PgDn
Scroll the panels, one at a time, when the window is too short for all of
them (the mouse wheel outside the sensor table and process list does too).
.TP
.B 1\(en9, v
Show or hide panels; \fBv\fR opens a list where panels can also be moved
between columns and reordered.
.TP
.B c
Compact mode.
.TP
.B t, T
Pick a color scheme (live preview), or switch to the next one.
.TP
.B u
Toggle \(deC / \(deF.
.TP
.B + \-
Refresh interval up or down by 100 ms.
.TP
.B s, r
Sort sensors by name or temperature; reset min/max.
.TP
.B l, L
Write everything shown (header, every sensor, each visible panel) to
\fI/tmp/oryn\-<date>\-<time>.log\fR, readable by you only.
.TP
.B p, n
Process sort order; next network interface.
.PP
In the process list: \fBf\fR or \fB/\fR filter, \fBe\fR start a command,
\fBt\fR terminate, \fBk\fR kill, \fBn\fR set nice.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/oryn/
Saved theme, panels, layout and compact mode.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sensors (1),
.BR smartctl (8),
.BR btop (1)
.PP
